# Everything the build makes for itself, or must not carry into an image.
#
# node_modules first and twice: the host's is built for the host's platform and its native
# modules would be the wrong architecture inside the container, which fails at load time
# rather than at build time. The build stage installs its own.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. The image builds from source, so anything here is stale by definition.
dist
**/dist
**/dev-dist
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report

# Somebody's data and somebody's secrets, neither of which belongs in a layer anyone can pull.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data
backups
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.pem
*.key

# History and tooling. .git alone is most of the build context in a repository this size.
.git
.github
.idea
.vscode
docs

# The image's own files. Changing the Compose file must not invalidate the build cache.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
Caddyfile
